	<!--
	  Direct carriage (Kurswagen) modelled with JourneyParts.

	  Source situation - the direct-carriage example of the SKI HRDF realisation
	  guide, section 7.1.4:

	    *KW  000037
	    *KWZ 000472 80____ Zuerich HB    - Basel Bad Bf   02215 02319
	    *KWZ 000470 80____ Basel Bad Bf  - Hannover Hbf   02340 00612
	    *KWZ 002746 80____ Hannover Hbf  - Bremen Hbf     00644 00754

	  Model: the coach group is one complete ServiceJourney from Zuerich HB to
	  Bremen Hbf - that is what a passenger books. It is divided into three
	  JourneyParts, one per pulling train. Each part says, through
	  ParentJourneyRef, which original journey the coach is attached to, and
	  through FromPointInPatternRef / ToPointInPatternRef where it rides along in
	  that journey's own ServiceJourneyPattern. This mirrors *KWZ one to one.

	  Train 470 continues from Hannover Hbf to Hamburg-Altona after the coach group
	  has been detached. Its JourneyPart therefore covers only points 1 to 2 of the
	  three-point pattern of 470 - a real sub-range, not the whole parent pattern.

	  JourneyPartCoupleRef is not used: ParentJourneyRef together with the two
	  PointInPattern references already states which train pulls which section.

	  See uc08_kurswagen.md.
	-->
